  "protocol_review": {
    "system_one": "22 suites, with one accuracy per suite. MIRACL listwise and pairwise use disjoint queries (build_arabic.py usable[:N] vs usable[N:2*N]); typed-decisions counted once, omitting type/workflow/overall aggregates. Fixed choice baselines reviewed against builder; variable-arity and grounding use no chance correction. Image and text screenshots are correlated modalities, not new independent studies.",
    "agent": "Three distinct levels/datasets; no L3 agent success, no overlapping BFCL-only or must-ask subgroup. Named v1.4 Verdict and v2.1 Decider attach to the corresponding existing JevBench identities, connecting that group without transferring weights or guessing revisions.",
    "failed": "All-request Tev1 Banking77 protocol unsupported (77 labels exceeds endpoint cap 20): preserved but invalid. Other failed requests retain publisher all-request denominators.",
    "identity": "Published exact named models/API slugs in site/meta.json and AgentDecisionBench models.jsonl. Local System One results are llama.cpp Q8_0 configurations, explicitly recorded; they do not replace native/BF16 observations. Endpoint observations retain requested release names; no served weight hash is invented."
  },
